WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.560
Texas Republicans seem to have a thing about&nbsp;
volunteering other people to do things that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.800
maybe they don't want to do. Remember back&nbsp;
in the earlier phases of the virus in Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.720
when Texas Republican Lieutenant Governor&nbsp;
Dan Patrick went on TV and said, listen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:23.360
grandma would sacrifice herself to save the&nbsp;
economy by which he really meant the stock market.&nbsp;

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.760
And then we said, well, grandma&nbsp;
isn't Dan Patrick's to sacrifice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.760
now, former Texas Republican governor and&nbsp;
former Trump secretary of energy Rick Perry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.600
is saying Texans are willing to continue going&nbsp;
without power so that the federal government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.960
doesn't get involved in their energy market.
It's not his role to decide who wants to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.769
without power. In a blog that was posted&nbsp;
on House Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.769 --> 00:00:55.120
his website, Rick Perry wrote, quote, Texans would&nbsp;
be without electricity for longer than three days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.240
to keep the federal government out of&nbsp;
their business. How does he know that?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.800
Try not to let whatever the crisis&nbsp;
of the day is, take your eye off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.280
of having a resilient grid that keeps America&nbsp;
safe personally, economically and strategically.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.880
Personal responsibility, right?
Rick Perry can say what he wants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:21.680
what he's willing to do, but who is he to say how&nbsp;
many days other Texans are willing to go without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:29.760
power or heat or water for political reasons? What&nbsp;
he is saying here is some of you may die to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:35.840
our power unregulated by the federal government,&nbsp;
but that's a sacrifice I am volunteering you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:42.080
to make, what for people who maybe aren't&nbsp;
up to speed on this issue. Understandably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:48.112
Texas has a power power grid that's run by&nbsp;
I believe the acronym is Bercot Earshot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.960
And it's the only power grid in the United States&nbsp;
that doesn't cross state lines. And as a result of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.680
that, it's not under the oversight of the Federal&nbsp;
Energy Regulatory Commission. Rick Perry likes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:06.080
that. A lot of Texas Republican elected officials&nbsp;
like that. And what Rick Perry is saying here is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.480
because he wants to keep that going, it's the&nbsp;
equivalent of saying, listen, Americans are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:17.120
willing to have an extra 50000 extra 50000 people&nbsp;
die of covid so that we don't get controlled by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.920
the WHL or something like that. That's essentially&nbsp;
the equivalent of what Rick Perry is saying. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:28.800
first of all, I doubt it from everybody I'm&nbsp;
talking to in Texas. Nobody, even libertarians and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.800
other people, nobody seems OK with what's going&nbsp;
on so that they can maintain their independence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:40.080
from any other grids and federal oversight.&nbsp;
Secondly, it's not Rick Perry's call to make.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:48.560
If there is a power outage, others are willing&nbsp;
to die for Rick Perry's separatist views. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:52.480
that that's that that just can't be.&nbsp;
And one other thing on this I've said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:59.600
despite the hypocrisy of Texas Republicans like&nbsp;
Ted Cruz demanding federal relief money for Texas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:05.120
now, but was against federal relief money when&nbsp;
it was needed in New York and New Jersey for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.480
Hurricane Sandy, despite him being a disgusting&nbsp;
hypocrite. I don't want Texans to go without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.160
federal aid. I still want the people of&nbsp;
Texas to get the relief money because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.760
they need it. I don't want to hold it back&nbsp;
from them because Ted Cruz is a hypocrite.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.480
But there is a real question here about if&nbsp;
Texas refuses to become part of a bigger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:28.000
broader, interstate resilient power grid, should&nbsp;
they continue to be bailed out by the feds?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.560
There are options for preventing this by being&nbsp;
part of a multi state power grid, and they refuse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.320
but then they still want the money when it fails.&nbsp;
Again, I don't want to deny the people of Texas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.880
anything, but shouldn't someone make it clear&nbsp;
to Texas, you've got to join us. If you want us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.280
to bail you out, you have to join the power grid&nbsp;
because otherwise you're bringing this problem on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:52.480
yourselves. They had power outages in 2011 for&nbsp;
similar reasons. They got a report telling them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.200
how to prevent this from happening again. They&nbsp;
didn't do anything that the report said. And now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:03.040
they immediately and defiantly say, give us the&nbsp;
cash. There has to be some limit at some point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:08.000
And somebody needs to sit Ted Cruz down and&nbsp;
talk about it. Except Ted Cruz flew to Cancun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.080
in the middle of all of this.&nbsp;
I want to talk about that next

